<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Pack with a CURRENT nuget.exe:  nuget pack DataverseErdVisualizer.nuspec
  (never `dotnet pack` — it regenerates the dependency list from the csproj
  and replaces the required literal `XrmToolBox` dependency id).

  Portal rules learned the hard way on Dataverse Process Mapper:
  - dependency id must be the literal `XrmToolBox` (not XrmToolBoxPackage)
  - layout must be lib\net48\Plugins\<dll> with third-party DLLs in a
    lib\net48\Plugins\DataverseErdVisualizer\ subfolder
  - <summary> and a non-empty <releaseNotes> are required; NO <license> element
  - <iconUrl> must be a public, reachable image URL
  - package version must equal the assembly <Version> in the csproj
  - the portal validates ALL listed versions: unlist any bad ones on nuget.org
-->
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2011/08/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>CasasHern.DataverseErdVisualizer</id>
    <version>1.6.0</version>
    <title>Dataverse ERD Visualizer</title>
    <authors>Cristian Casas</authors>
    <owners>casashern</owners>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/caschern/Dataverse-ERD-Visualizer</projectUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/caschern/Dataverse-ERD-Visualizer/main/images/icon.png</iconUrl>
    <icon>images\icon.png</icon>
    <summary>Generate interactive Entity Relationship Diagrams from any Dataverse solution.</summary>
    <description>XrmToolBox tool that generates interactive Entity Relationship Diagrams from a selected Dataverse solution: tables, columns, lookups and N:N relationships in crow's-foot notation. Hide system noise, drag tables to fine-tune the layout, inspect any table's columns and relationships, and export to PNG, SVG, PDF, an HTML data dictionary or a Mermaid erDiagram.</description>
    <releaseNotes>Row wrapping: a row of tables wider than the rest of the diagram now has tables moved down into the rows below, and long connectors leaving the same table share one bundled trunk instead of each reserving its own channel (Options - Wrap wide rows). Satellite grids above a deeply nested hub now always sit directly above it. Focus mode: right-click any table to show just its neighbourhood (direct relationships, or two hops), with a Show all tables button to come back - the way to explore a model too large to read at once. Tables you drag now stay where you put them: manual positions survive rebuilds and are remembered per solution between sessions, with Options - Reset manual layout to clear them. A table with a many-to-many relationship to itself is now described as such in the knowledge base instead of as a lookup hierarchy. Self-referential (hierarchy) relationships now state their cascade behaviour, and the per-table knowledge base export writes into its own solution-named subfolder, warning about leftover files from an earlier run. Documentation now includes what agents and analysts actually ask for: every column carries its description and, for choice, status and yes/no columns, the full list of allowed values with their stored numbers; every relationship carries its cascade behaviour in plain English ("deleting Contact records clears the Assigned Judge lookup on related Case records"). Shown in the knowledge base exports, the HTML data dictionary and the table details pane. Earlier: new Export submenu "Knowledge base for AI agents" (Copilot Studio and similar): export one Markdown file per table plus an overview, or a single combined file. Relationships are written out from both sides, columns are self-describing bullets that survive chunk splits, and no diagram is embedded. Satellite clustering now recognises tables that carry several lookups to the same hub (they show one connector marked "xN", or every relationship when you tick the option). Satellite table clustering: tables whose only relationship is to one hub are packed into a compact grid beside it, so hub-heavy solutions no longer render as diagrams tens of thousands of pixels wide (toggle under Options). Also: per-relationship connector ports with rotated labels, drag-to-reposition that preserves connector routing, and PNG / SVG / PDF / HTML data dictionary / Mermaid erDiagram export.</releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright 2026 Cristian Casas</copyright>
    <tags>XrmToolBox Dataverse ERD Diagram Metadata PowerPlatform Dynamics365</tags>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="XrmToolBox" version="1.2025.10.74" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="bin\Release\DataverseErdVisualizer.dll" target="lib\net48\Plugins" />
    <file src="bin\Release\PdfSharp.dll" target="lib\net48\Plugins\DataverseErdVisualizer" />
    <file src="bin\Release\PdfSharp.Charting.dll" target="lib\net48\Plugins\DataverseErdVisualizer" />
    <file src="images\icon.png" target="images" />
  </files>
</package>
